        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12447021/comment/12867087",
          "id": "12867087",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=martinblech",
            "name": "martinblech",
            "key": "martinblech",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Martin Blech",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "It is causing an issue in a JAX-RS application that uses Sun's Jersey reference implementation and is deployed on the Grizzly servlet container. Apparently, Grizzly's ThreadPool implemenation uses Thread.interrupt() extensively.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=martinblech",
            "name": "martinblech",
            "key": "martinblech",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Martin Blech",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2010-05-13T08:50:45.000+0000",
          "updated": "2010-05-13T08:50:45.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12447021/comment/12902068",
          "id": "12902068",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "By the way, seems like this affects MMapDirectory too.\n\nant test-core -Dtestcase=TestIndexWriter -Dtestmethod=testThreadInterruptDeadlock -Dtests.directory=MMapDirectory\n\n{noformat}\n    [junit] ------------- Standard Output ---------------\n    [junit] FAILED; unexpected exception\n    [junit] java.nio.channels.ClosedByInterruptException\n    [junit]     at java.nio.channels.spi.AbstractInterruptibleChannel.end(AbstractInterruptibleChannel.java:184)\n    [junit]     at sun.nio.ch.FileChannelImpl.map(FileChannelImpl.java:772)\n{noformat}\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2010-08-24T21:02:58.180+0000",
          "updated": "2010-08-24T21:02:58.180+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12447021/comment/12902073",
          "id": "12902073",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=simonw",
            "name": "simonw",
            "key": "simonw",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Simon Willnauer",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "bq. By the way, seems like this affects MMapDirectory too.\nAll AbstractInterruptibleChannel subclasses are affected unfortunately. We should at least document it in the java docs.\n\nsimon\n\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=simonw",
            "name": "simonw",
            "key": "simonw",
            "avatarUrls": {
